{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524941-true-vtm-bloodlines-successor","id":1524941,"title":"True VtM:Bloodlines successor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-02T16:44:27-07:00","id":1524941,"title":"True VtM:Bloodlines successor","content":"It is becoming clear that the new Bloodlines 2 game being made by the Chinese Room studio and published by Paradox is actually nothing like the well beloved VtM:Bloodlines game.<br /> <br /> How I would love if Onyx Path partnered with a game studio for a VtR game that is the true spiritual successor to Bloodlines 1.<br /> <br /> I'd pay AAA price for it, honestly.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bMy wishlist would be:<ul><li>Requiem setting, obviously</li> <li>Deus Ex like gameplay, with lots of environment clues that tie into the story</li> <li>A Dragon Age Origins prologue style, one for each clan, that establishes the player character and their relationship with the game world</li> <li>At least one truly terrifying mission/quest. Bloodlines 1 had a couple really spooky moments that I remember fondly even though I don't usually like horror games</li> <li>Native modding support. I don't mean modding tools, just support for custom code to be loaded into the game. Modders are the reason Bloodlines 1 had a real life and cult following as the official game was a nightmare of bugs.</li> </ul><br /> I've read every single Requiem book since 1E but never actually played a full chronicle due to life challenges and difficulties finding a group that takes the setting seriously. Having a VtR game is maybe my only chance to really be part of the setting...<br /> <br /> Please, Onyx Path, take this opportunity that Bloodlines 2 will most likely leave most fans of the original game with a bad taste in mouth, and move in to offer a true successor!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2611-guiskj","name":"guiskj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2611_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T18:08:20-07:00","id":1524948,"title":"","content":"c'mon man, this is unnecessary and quite rude","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T18:19:15-07:00","id":1524950,"title":"","content":"In what way? I'd like to understand, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2611-guiskj","name":"guiskj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2611_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T18:33:06-07:00","id":1524951,"title":"","content":"Onyx Path isn't even being allowed to make new books, you honestly think they would be allowed to make a video game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T18:36:54-07:00","id":1524952,"title":"","content":"I thought they owned the rights to nWoD. I've been away for quite some time, so I'm not up to date with any embargo. I thought the books stop being made because of a general PnP slump...<br /> <br /> This is sad news indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2611-guiskj","name":"guiskj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2611_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T08:00:07-07:00","id":1524975,"title":"","content":"Since dreaming is free for everyone - and I'm also not confident Bloodline 2 will be what I'm expecting from this game, even though the hope is always alive - here my view of how I'd like to have a vampire's game set up in 2024:<br /> <br /> - free roaming map<br /> -similar jumping mechanic to Spiderman's serie (automatic jumps, or charged jump) with distance parameterized by the combination of Str+atlh+Vigor (with the basic distance multiplied by the discipline itself (obviously with different flavor of movements, more dark and less comic oriented).<br /> - Possibility to climb wall as Assassin creed (the first of the series, or Infamous), with reachable range determined by Strght/dexterity?+Athl+vig<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">-Possibility to unlock wall climbing as spiderman's serie when acquiring Protean 2</div> - Celerity which allow to dash away or through enemies<br /> - Mental disciplines that allows for both in combat and out of combat/dialogue capabilities. <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">- in combat it may be similar to what seen in the Witcher 3</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">- Out of combat gives more dialogue options, helps the result of a dialogue (like Baldur's Gate 3), or give a contextual menu with 3 or 4 options depending on the discipline used on any NPC: </div><div style=\"margin-left:80px\">- follow me; go away; yell, attack etc</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">would be cool if the mission/level design would allow for several approaches to the same situation (depending on also powers used) like Dishonored 2 allowed</div> - mood and atmosphere dark and creepy (although variegate).<br /> <br /> But I'm aware this kind of game would require a AAA studio. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T22:51:17-07:00","id":1525012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guiskj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524941-true-vtm-bloodlines-successor#post1524941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is becoming clear that the new Bloodlines 2 game being made by the Chinese Room studio and published by Paradox is actually nothing like the well beloved VtM:Bloodlines game.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bMy wishlist would be:<ul><li>Requiem setting, obviously</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the asinine nitpickery, but it's quite difficult to speak of a Requiem-inspired game as &quot;true&quot; VtM:Bloodlines sucessor, by simple virtue of the fact that the original Bloodlines was part of the Masquerade, with its different clans, lore and etc.<br /> <br /> Just that makes a straight port or sequel impossible, since a lot of elements of the game do not exist or fit in Requiem as given - damn, a number of elements of Bloodlines don't fit with Masquerade in its last iterations (hello Cathayans/Kuei-jin/whatever), for that matter!\u200b<br /> <br /> Not even going into the slippery slope of the knee-jerk reaction a not insignificant fraction of VtM fans have always had to Requiem, that's a whole different can of worms to open. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All of that said, the base set-up of Bloodlines, of an illegally freshly-embraced neonate whose sire is destroyed for the infraction but gets itself spared from Final Death only to be turned into the Prince's newest legbreaker, <b>can</b> be used pretty fine for a game based in the Requiem setting. Some of the questlines, that touched on the subjects of inter-sect conflict or noddist lore, might require some tweaking and ad hoc world-building for the sake of fitting in a way that made some sort of sense, but pretty doable i guess. Much of the cast too - speaking from experience there, as i used <b>a lot</b> of reskined Bloodlines NPCs for the cast of my own city while STing Requiem more than a decade ago.<br /> <br /> (Damn, spontaneous rising is even a thing in Requiem, so something like the Cathayans would be much more setting compatible than it ever was in Masquerade)<br /> <br /> Main difference overall would be that Gehenna/End Times narrative is in no way a major element of Requiem, while it does play a major role in Masquerade and a not insignificant part of the tone of the game - and the actions of a quite major character/antagonist, Prince Lacroix - hinge into the conceit of this &quot;sense of doom&quot; coming of the return of ancients (be it either Messerach or Caine).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guiskj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524941-true-vtm-bloodlines-successor#post1524941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read every single Requiem book since 1E but never actually played a full chronicle due to life challenges and difficulties finding a group that takes the setting seriously. Having a VtR game is maybe my only chance to really be part of the setting...</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have Discord? You could check out Onyx Path's Discord Community and try your luck at setting up an online group in there - that's how i got accidentally promoted to ST of a V20 game (that happens to be a partial spin-off of Bloodlines in fact) just a few months back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T23:15:49-08:00","id":1526440,"title":"","content":"&quot;Absolutely agree! A true VtR successor with Requiem setting, Deus Ex gameplay, and Dragon Age Origins-style prologues would be a dream. A nod to Bloodlines 1's spooky missions and native modding support would be fantastic. Onyx Path, consider seizing this opportunity for a game that captures the essence we all love!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28130-maricastaneda","name":"MariCastaneda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T03:00:15-08:00","id":1526550,"title":"","content":"I am excited for this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28047-lewisdavis","user":"LewisDavis","date":". 01-09-2024, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28047-lewisdavis","name":"LewisDavis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}